<section>
  <h2>About This Portal</h2>
  <p>
    The Pandharpur Wari is one of the largest annual pilgrimages, bringing together lakhs of devotees (warkaris)
    walking together towards Pandharpur. Despite its scale, pilgrims and remote devotees often lack easy access
    to information, navigation help, emergency support, and ways to participate digitally.
  </p>

  <h3>Problem Statement</h3>
  <p>
    Lack of accessible information, navigation, emergency support, and digital participation options reduces
    the overall experience and inclusiveness of the Pandharpur Wari.
  </p>

  <h3>Our Solution</h3>
  <p>
    This portal provides nearby facility information, emergency support, and a digital seva platform
    for remote devotees.
  </p>

  <h3>What You Can Do Here</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/facilities">Find nearby facilities</a> — medical camps, food, water, toilets, and shelter points along the route.</li>
    <li><a href="/emergency">Get emergency support</a> — helpline numbers and a quick form to report an emergency.</li>
    <li><a href="/seva">Participate in Digital Seva</a> — remote devotees can contribute to Annadan, medical seva, donations, and volunteering.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

